==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*swait-}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*swoyd-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{m|osx|swêt}}, Old High German {{m|goh|sweiz}}, Old Norse {{m|non|sveiti||sweat, blood}}. The Indo-European root also gave Latin {{m|la|sudor}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|स्वेद}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/swɑːt/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m|head=swāt}}

# [[blood]]

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|en|swate}}, {{l|en|swote}}, {{l|en|swot}}, {{l|enm|swete}}, {{l|enm|swet}}
** English: {{l|en|sweat}}

